    "narrative": "For Ghost Ride the WHIP on this June 18th slate, our offensive ceiling is anchored by **Josh Naylor** (66.95) and **Tyler Soderstrom** (66.42), our two highest-scoring assets. **Josh Naylor** benefits from a favorable matchup against Shane Baz; despite a neutral park adjustment, the combination of his #3 spot in the order and a positive platoon split against the right-hander makes him our primary anchor. Similarly, **Tyler Soderstrom** earns his high efficiency score largely due to a lucrative park factor and the premium associated with his assumed #3 spot, even in the absence of a confirmed opposing starter. **Austin Riley** (60.43) also stands out as a strong start, with an outfield wind blowing out adding a 5% boost to his projection, effectively offsetting the minor risk posed by a strong defensive catcher.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision involved **Travis Bazzana**, who narrowly missed the starting cut with a 34.68 score. While his potential to lead off (a 10% boost) is enticing, his current matchup against Shane Drohan is heavily suppressed by a negative SP skill adjustment and a detrimental L/L platoon disadvantage, forcing us to bench him to preserve our limited game caps. We are also closely monitoring the lineup for **Jose Caballero** (54.21); while he offers crucial speed upside, his score was hit by a 13% penalty due to the platoon dynamics against Sean Burke. We are operating with a heightened sense of caution regarding our remaining lineup slots, as **Brice Turang**, **Max Muncy**, **Cole Young**, and **Henry Bolte** all rely on pending lineup confirmations to maintain their projected value. We remain sidelined on **Corbin Carroll** due to a scheduled day off, while **Vinnie Pasquantino** and **Mickey Moniak** remain unavailable as they continue their stints on the IL.",
